> violate any of the rules requires the rafsi prefix to end in a consonant.
> If you allow CVV- and CCV- as prefixes, then stage 3 fu'ivla can no longe=
r
> be made easily on the fly.
>
> In any case, it doesn't really matter what one calls valid fu'ivla that
> start with CVVrC- or CCVrC-. Whatever one calls them, they cannot be made
> as easily on the fly as those that start with CCVCrC-, CVCCrC- or CVCrC,
>

